# PSR-5g — Identity admin client (closes ALW-ID)

## Why

`user` / `mobileOtpChallenge` (and related pre-tenant identity I/O) use FORCE RLS
with no `app_tour` policies — admin pool remains required. PSR-5 item 5 still
demands a **named** access path with reason codes, not raw `getPrismaAdmin` in
the repository.

## Design (behavior-preserving)

Thin client (same shape as platform/background clients — safer than extracting
every Prisma shape into a port in one wave):

`apps/api/src/identity/identity-admin-client.ts`

| Piece | Detail |
| --- | --- |
| API | `getIdentityAdminClient(reason)` |
| Metric | `identity_admin_access_total{reason}` |
| Pool | still `getPrismaAdmin()` — **only** inside the client |
| Consumer | `prisma-identity.repository.ts` — zero direct admin |

### Reason codes (5)

| Reason | Sites |
| --- | --- |
| `ID_USER_READ` | findUserByMobile / ById / ByIds; post-update reload |
| `ID_USER_WRITE` | registerPublicGuest create; updateUserMobile transaction |
| `ID_OTP` | create / find / mark OTP challenge |
| `ID_PENDING_INVITE` | findPendingInviteForAccept |
| `ID_SESSION_BUMP` | cross-tenant `userTenant.sessionVersion` increment |

## Allowlist

`ALW-ID-FORCE-RLS` **closed** — sole owner is `identity-admin-client.ts`.
PSR-5b active allowlist entry count → **0**.

## Non-goals

- Changing FORCE RLS / policies
- Dual-store cleanup (item 6)
- Same-SHA proofs (item 7)
- Rewriting identity business logic

## Smoke

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-5g-identity-admin-smoke.mjs
node scripts/ops/psr-5b-admin-allowlist-smoke.mjs
node scripts/ops/psr-5-data-authority-inventory-smoke.mjs
```
